first 300: The Lighthouse Operator's Handbook\n\nby Harriet Pemberton\n\nChapter 1: First Principles\n\nEvery coastal watchtower demands attention to three things above all else: the mechanism that drives the lens, the fuel that feeds the flame, and the log that records each passing vessel. Without any one of these,
last 300: d) means "I am taking in, or discharging, or carrying dangerous goods."\n\nThis handbook serves as a foundation. No written guide replaces the judgment built through seasons of direct experience at the post. Trust the instruments, trust the training, and above all, trust what the sea itself tells you.
